# Chat Persistence and GPT-4 Mini Implementation

## Problem Analysis

1. Current Issues:
   - Chat history is not persisted between API calls
   - Using GPT-4 instead of GPT-4-mini model
   - Each API call starts a fresh conversation
   - No service layer for chat functionality

2. Affected Components:
   - `app/src/app/api/chat/route.ts`
   - `app/src/components/chat/chat-interface.tsx`
   - `app/src/services/chat/chat.service.ts` (to be created)
   - `app/src/types/chat.ts` (to be created)

3. Performance Implications:
   - Memory usage for storing conversation history
   - API response time with context
   - Service layer abstraction overhead

## Solution Design

1. Service Layer Implementation:
   - Create ChatService class
   - Implement singleton pattern
   - Handle OpenAI configuration
   - Manage conversation context
   - Provide error handling

2. Conversation Persistence:
   - Use client-side state management for current session
   - Pass full conversation history in API calls
   - Implement proper message structuring

3. GPT-4 Mini Migration:
   - Update OpenAI API configuration in service
   - Test response quality
   - Monitor performance differences

## Implementation Steps

- [x] Create Service Layer
  - [x] Define chat types and interfaces
  - [x] Implement ChatService class
  - [x] Add error handling and logging
  - Success criteria: Working service with proper abstraction ✓

- [x] Update OpenAI Configuration
  - [x] Change model to GPT-4-mini in service
  - [x] Test basic responses
  - Success criteria: Successful API responses with new model ✓

- [x] Implement Conversation Persistence
  - [x] Modify message handling in chat interface
  - [x] Update API route to use ChatService
  - [x] Add proper error handling
  - Success criteria: Continuous conversation context between messages ✓

